.TH FAAD 1 "2026-10-02" "2.2.0" "Free AAC Decoder"

.SH NAME
faad \- open source MPEG-4 and MPEG-2 AAC decoder

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B faad
.RI [ options ]
.RI [\-o\  outfile ]
.I infile
.PP
.RI < infile >
is an ADTS
.B .aac
stream or an MP4
.B .m4a
file.

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B FAAD
is an open source MPEG-4 and MPEG-2 AAC decoder, it is licensed under the LGPL license.
It decodes AAC-LC and HE-AAC v1 (SBR) streams, and HE-AAC v2 (PS) when built with
parametric stereo support, to PCM.
By default the output is a WAV file named after the input;
.B -w
or
.B -f raw
write to standard output or omit the header.

.SH I/O AND FORMAT OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -o ,\  --output\ <\fIfile\fP>
Set output filename (default: stdout if piped, or the input name with a
.B .wav
extension).
.TP
.BR -w ,\  --stdout
Write output PCM to stdout.
.TP
.BR -f ,\  --format\ <\fItype\fP>
Output container format: wav (default) or raw.
.TP
.BR -b ,\  --bits\ <\fIdepth\fP>
Sample depth: 16 (default), 24 or 32f (32-bit float).
.TP
.BR -a ,\  --adts\ <\fIfile\fP>
Extract the raw ADTS stream from an MP4 file without decoding.

.SH PROCESSING OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -d ,\  --downmix\ [\fImode\fP]
Downmix audio to mono (mono or 1, the default) or stereo (stereo or 2).
.TP
.BR -j ,\  --jump\ <\fIseconds\fP>
Start decoding from the specified timestamp.
.TP
.BR -g ,\  --no-gapless
Disable automatic gapless trim and padding handling.

.SH INFORMATION AND GENERAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -i ,\  --info
Display bitstream and container metadata, then exit.
.TP
.BR --json
Output the bitstream information in JSON format.
.TP
.BR -q ,\  --quiet
Quiet mode, suppress decoding progress.
.TP
.BR --strict
Strict mode, report errors noisily with debug details on failure.
.TP
.BR --license
Display copyright and license information.
.TP
.BR -h ,\  --help
Display a short help text.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR faac (1)

